# =========================================================================
# tools/mod — tool registry and execution.
#
# Parity oracle: rust-old/src/tools/mod.rs
#
# Tools are the actions agents can perform. In the oracle every tool implements
# the `NativeTool` trait and lives in a `DashMap`-backed registry; here a tool
# is a small function-pointer vtable and the registry is a hashmap behind a
# futex mutex. Both changes are forced — Cyrius has neither traits nor a
# concurrent map — and both are documented at the top of their modules.
#
# Include order is a dependency constraint (resolution is single-pass):
# tools_registry calls into tools_native, and both use core_json's helpers, so
# `src/core/mod.cyr` must precede this hub. src/main.cyr does that.
#
# PORT IN PROGRESS:
#   * native   — done (schemas, input, output, the tool vtable)
#   * registry — done (registration, lookup, allow-list gating, the mutex)
#   * builtin/echo + builtin/json_transform — done (tools_builtin_basic)
#   * builtin/load_testing — done. It is the first module to use the blocker #3
#     per-worker arena pattern for real: one OS thread per simulated user, each
#     with a persistent arena for its latencies and a scratch arena reset after
#     every request.
#   * builtin/security_audit — done. Split at the network boundary so the
#     oracle's mock-server tests port without loopback, which is_safe_url
#     rightly refuses.
#   * builtin/{synapse,mneme,delta} — done. Nine tools with one shape, so the
#     shape lives once in tools_agnos.cyr rather than nine times. These are the
#     one tool family that must NOT run the SSRF guard: they target loopback
#     services by design, and the guard would reject every default base URL.
#   * remote_registry — done. A guarded fetch, which is all the oracle ever
#     was: its doc comment promises ZIP/WASM handling and registration, but the
#     file contains none of it and has zero consumers.
#
#   * python_tool — done, M11. An adapter over `src/sandbox/python.cyr`, which
#     M7 had already ported whole; only the vtable binding and the
#     stdout-to-`ToolOutput` ladder were missing.
#
# ⚠ This paragraph used to read "Deferred with their features … `python_tool.rs`,
# `wasm_tool.rs` and `wasm_loader.rs`. WASM as a format is an explicit cyrius
# non-goal". **Retired.** A cargo feature gate is not a scope boundary, and
# ADR-006's own 2026-08-07 correction overturned the WASM half of it: kavach
# ships a wasmtime backend with fuel, memory bounds and preopens, so
# `wasm_tool.rs` and `wasm_loader.rs` have successors rather than substitutes.
#
#   * wasm_tool, wasm_loader — done, M11, on `src/sandbox/wasm.cyr` and kavach
#     3.11.8's backend per [ADR 019](../../docs/adr/019-wasm-tools-spawn-wasmtime-directly.md).
# =========================================================================

include "src/tools/native.cyr"
include "src/tools/python_tool.cyr"
include "src/tools/wasm_tool.cyr"
include "src/tools/wasm_loader.cyr"
include "src/tools/registry.cyr"
include "src/tools/builtin/basic.cyr"
include "src/tools/builtin/load_testing.cyr"
include "src/tools/agnos.cyr"
include "src/tools/builtin/security_audit.cyr"
include "src/tools/builtin/synapse.cyr"
include "src/tools/builtin/mneme.cyr"
include "src/tools/builtin/delta.cyr"
include "src/tools/remote_registry.cyr"
